<template>
    <children>
        <li id="28.lp5"/>
    </children>
    <heading>Operations</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>operations</li>
        <li>generator</li>
        <li>coroutine</li>
        <li>command handler</li>
        <li>initialization</li>
        <li>to_handler</li>
        <li>modal dialog</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>operations</code> holds the application's multi-step command handlers. Each handler is a generator object, created and primed by <code>to_handler</code>. The generator receives <code>self</code>, a function that returns its own object; calling <code>self()</code> after construction avoids accessing the object before it exists.</p>
        <p>Each operation can produce one of three outcomes when <code>controller</code> resumes it with <code>handler.next(command)</code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><code>yield self()</code>: remain the current handler. The controller stops dispatching this command; the next command resumes the same operation.</li>
            <li><code>yield child</code>, where <code>child</code> is another primed generator object: call a child operation. The controller pushes <code>child</code> onto <code>handlerStack</code> and immediately dispatches the same command to it.</li>
            <li><code>return</code>, or reach the end of the generator: finish the operation. The generator result has <code>done === true</code>, so the controller pops it and resumes the parent with the same command. Any returned value is ignored. If no parent remains, dispatch ends.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>A <code>ModalDialog</code> command carries a <code>dialogName</code> key identifying the dialog-specific operation. The base handler switches on that key and yields the selected primed operation. The controller then sends the same initial command to the child.</p>
        <p><code>SelectCreateProject</code> is the operation for the startup project dialog. It receives the initial command and calls <code>view.showModalDialog</code> with the dialog template's DOM id. The view mounts and displays the dialog, then returns immediately. The operation remains the active handler and can receive later commands while the dialog is open.</p>
        <p>The Select button dispatches <code>SelectProject</code> immediately. Its child handler starts the nested <code>asyncSelectProject</code> function before its priming yield, invoking the local picker during user activation, or opening the supplied remote URL without a picker. The generator then waits throughout selection, persistence, and loading, ignoring unrelated commands. <code>ProjectPickerAborted</code> finishes the child and leaves the dialog available; all fatal errors escape to global error handling.</p>
        <p><code>ProjectLoaded</code> finishes the child. The controller resumes the parent at its child yield with that same command. The parent closes and removes the dialog, then finishes. Rendering the loaded model is the next unfinished step. The Create operation remains an unwritten bundle, and its button is not wired.</p>
        <p><code>operations</code> installs the primed base handler with <code>controller.init(handler)</code> before any commands are dispatched.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>JavaScript units</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
let operations = (() => {
    function to_handler(generator, ...args) {
        const handler = generator(() => handler, ...args);
        handler.next();
        return handler;
    }

    function* SelectProject(self, selection) {
        ]]><lp5- ref="SelectProject async work"/><![CDATA[
        asyncSelectProject(selection);

        // Priming; the next resume receives the initiating SelectProject command.
        yield;
        while (true) {
            const command = yield self();
            switch (command.name) {
            case "ProjectLoaded":
                return;
            case "ProjectPickerAborted":
                // AbortError does not distinguish dismissal from denied access.
                return;
            }
        }
    }

    function* SelectCreateProject(self) {
        let command = yield self();
        view.showModalDialog("SelectCreateProject");
        while (true) {
            command = yield self();
            switch (command.name) {
            case "SelectProject":
                command = yield to_handler(SelectProject, command);
                if (command.name === "ProjectLoaded") {
                    view.closeModalDialog("SelectCreateProject");
                    // TODO: Ask the view to render the loaded model.
                    return;
                }
                break;
            case "Create":
                yield ]]><lp5- ref="CreateProjectOperation"/><![CDATA[;
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    function* baseOperationsHandler(self) {
        while (true) {
            let command = yield self();
            if (command.name === "ModalDialog") {
                switch (command.dialogName) {
                case "SelectCreateProject":
                    yield to_handler(SelectCreateProject);
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    const handler = to_handler(baseOperationsHandler);
    controller.init(handler);

    return {};
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
